graded tree: c1eb31f530bd  (810 files: crates fixtures scripts, content-hashed)
  1 gitignored byproduct file(s) under those directories were NOT hashed
  (board #3048; it was 0 at the start of this run). The subtraction is
  printed at BOTH ends on purpose: a denominator nobody prints on both sides of a
  change is a denominator that grows unwatched (#1002). A rise here is not a failure —
  it is the gate saying which of its own byproducts it declined to grade itself on.
  This is the identity of what was graded. It is a hash of file CONTENT, not
  a commit — HEAD is what lied in #2907, and a commit id is silent about
  uncommitted work, a half-restored tree and a concurrent writer alike.
